    <rdfs:label>anatomical cluster</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>anatomical cluster</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>Anatomical structure, which has as its parts a heterogeneous collection of  organs, organ parts, cells, cell parts or body part subdivisions that are adjacent to, or continuous with one another; does not constitute a cell part, cell,  tissue,  organ, organ system or organ system subdivision, cardinal body part, body part subdivision or anatomical junction. Examples: joint, adnexa of uterus, root of lung, renal pedicle, back.</skos:definition>
    <cde:localId>AL-000105</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>AnatomicLocation</cde:nodeType>
