    <rdfs:label>zone of adrenal gland</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>A gross anatomic zone of the adrenal gland, as distinguished on cross-sectional imaging.</skos:definition>
    <cde:localId>AL-L0006</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>AnatomicLocation</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:source>local</cde:source>
    <cde:sourceStatus>pending_request</cde:sourceStatus>
    <cde:changeRequest>RADLEX-REQ-0640</cde:changeRequest>
    <cde:designNote>The kind an adrenal scope refines to. RadLex has no gross zoning of the gland: it carries the histological zonae, the cortex and medulla, and a childless limb concept, none of which is what a radiologist describes.</cde:designNote>
